- **Objective:** Review the full `git diff` across `synccli.py` and `test_synccli.py` against every constraint in `GOAL.md` and `README.md`; route any `minor` findings back to the `cheap-code` `task_id` followed by a fresh `cheap-review` pass, or report to the user before escalating any `major` finding.
- **Files to create/modify:** None (read-only).
- **Pipeline agent:** `review` (concrete agent: `cheap-review`, fresh session).
- **Risks:**
  - Overlooked edge cases in nested relative path formatting, Unicode filenames in `json.dumps`, or CLI argument order (`--json --dry-run` vs `--dry-run --json`).
  - Unintended modifications outside `synccli.py` and `test_synccli.py`.
- **Verifiable acceptance criterion:** `cheap-review` reports zero unresolved `major` or `minor` findings; `git diff --name-only` lists only `synccli.py` and `test_synccli.py`; zero third-party dependencies are present; all `TestSync` and new `--json`/`--dry-run` unit tests pass under Python 3.10+.
